{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לשבתך", :translit "lishbatkha", :gloss "for Your dwelling"} {:he "בנה בניתי בית זבול לך מכון לשבתך עולמים", :translit "bana baniti beit zevul lekha mekho'n l'shavtekha olamim", :gloss "a house I have built, a house of Zevul for You, a foundation for Your dwelling eternally"} {:he "מכון לשבתך", :translit "mekho'n lishbatkha", :gloss "a foundation for Your dwelling"} {:he "ירושלים ציון", :translit "yerushalayim tziyyon", :gloss "Jerusalem Zion"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["לשבתך" "מכון לשבתך"]} {:kind :gematria, :a "לשבתך", :b "ירושלים ציון"}], :frame {:text "The Temple below corresponds to a heavenly Temple above: as stated at Chagigah 12b, Zevul is identified as a heavenly sanctuary. Solomon's speech in 1 Kings 8:13 and its parallel formulation in 2 Chronicles 6:2 both employ the phrase מכון לשבתך, establishing the terrestrial Temple as a mirror of the celestial one.", :sources ["Chagigah 12b" "1 Kings 8:13" "2 Chronicles 6:2"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ידיך", :translit "yadekha", :gloss "Your hands"} {:he "יו\"ד יתירה", :translit "yod y'teirah", :gloss "extra yod"} {:he "י' נסים שנעשו במקדש", :translit "y' nesim sh'ne'asu bamikdash", :gloss "ten miracles that were done in the Temple"} {:he "י' קדושות שנתקדשה הארץ", :translit "y' kdushot shenitkadshah ha'aretz", :gloss "ten sanctities through which the land was sanctified"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The yod in the plural form ידיך (instead of singular ידך) is extra, standing for the number ten."}], :frame {:text "Ten miracles were regularly performed in the Temple, enumerated in Pirké de-Rabbi Eliezer 24 as part of the order of Temple service. The land of Israel was sanctified through ten decrees of sanctification, discussed in Mishnah Kelim 1:6–9, which catalogues ten levels of sanctity from the walls of Jerusalem inward to the Holy of Holies.", :sources ["Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 24" "Mishnah Kelim 1:6–9"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind